    "family_reading": {
        "text": "Mistral spans 12 versions, from Mistral Large in February 2024 to Mistral Medium 3.5 in April 2026. Across the whole family, 2 versions support reasoning and 5 publish open weights, so most are API only. Context windows run from 32768 to 262144 tokens, and inputs accept file, image and text, with text output. Prices vary widely: Mistral Nemo is cheapest at $0.02 input and $0.03 output per million tokens, while Mistral Medium 3.5 is the most expensive at $1.5 input and $7.5 output. The facts suggest the family suits long document and image work at many price points, with open weights available for some self hosting. Limits are that reasoning support is rare, and the largest context and output lengths sit in the pricier tiers.",
